1
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:38,220
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:40,810
[Episode 5]

3
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:42,560
Now look at yourself.

4
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:46,400
Do you think you're good enough
for Gu Han?

5
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:48,880
Explain yourself.

6
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,560
How am I not good enough for Gu Han?

7
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,479
What age are we living in?

8
00:01:51,479 --> 00:01:54,080
You're still pulling this
catfight nonsense.

9
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,160
Know your place.

10
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,720
Xiangxiang, you're so badass.

11
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:05,700
Don't be mad.

12
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:08,759
Explain yourself.

13
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,240
How am I not good enough for Gu Han?

14
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:12,100
I swear, it was exactly like that.

15
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:13,960
Xiangxiang,

16
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,040
I didn't know you had that in you.

17
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
So, I backed the right guy,

18
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,079
Gu Han, right?

19
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,079
I was just pissed off by Duan Xiaoyu.

20
00:02:22,079 --> 00:02:23,740
I was talking nonsense, okay?

21
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,760
Explaining is covering up.

22
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,160
If you didn't care about Gu Han,

23
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,600
would you be this mad?

24
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:29,400
Exactly.

25
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,640
I...

26
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:34,700
Welcome to the campus TV station.

27
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,720
I'm interning at the city TV station
these days.

28
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,079
Keep practicing with the station director

29
00:02:38,079 --> 00:02:39,079
and the teachers.

30
00:02:38,610 --> 00:02:39,940
[Senior Fang Yu]

31
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:39,910
Good luck.

32
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:43,070
Senior Fang Yu is starting
to report his schedule.

33
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:54,160
Don't spread what happened today.

34
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:01,920
What a tangled mess.

35
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,200
Explain yourself.

36
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,000
How am I not good enough for Gu Han?

37
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,120
Really?

38
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,360
Xiangxiang went off like that?

39
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,320
Why would I lie to you?

40
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,650
Her classmates said so.

41
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,280
It's 100% reliable.

42
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,200
How am I not good enough for Gu Han?

43
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,370
What does that mean?

44
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,620
Are you stupid?
You can't even understand that?

45
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,480
Don't you think Gu Han's been

46
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:31,200
giving off some special vibe today?

47
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,130
Vibe? What vibe?

48
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,840
He looks the same as usual.

49
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,920
Could this be the legendary

50
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,240
pre-romance vibe?

51
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:41,000
Why don't you get it yet?

52
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,840
-Chen Yu.
-You're so stupid.

53
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:44,840
Let's go.

54
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,560
Why are you sneaking around?

55
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,480
Then... I'll just say it.

56
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,200
Go on.

57
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,040
Did you do something to Xiangxiang?

58
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,970
How come she suddenly said
she's good enough for you?

59
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,880
You all have too much free time, huh?

60
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,079
Everyone, do 10 extra sets
of shuttle runs,

61
00:03:59,079 --> 00:04:00,000
and 200 shots.

62
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,160
Captain.

63
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:01,880
Go.

64
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,600
Let's go.

65
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,480
I have to go see Coach Pei.

66
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,120
Start.

67
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:11,840
Got it.

68
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,560
Before class meeting ends,

69
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,000
I have something to tell you.

70
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,560
Our College of Liberal Arts is holding

71
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,080
a sports meet next month.

72
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,800
The college really hopes

73
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,320
that our freshmen

74
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,880
will actively participate.

75
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:30,000
And there's a great incentive—

76
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:32,320
if you place, you'll get extra credits.

77
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,280
Isn't that great?

78
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:33,800
Great.

79
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,560
I'd rather just focus on classes.

80
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:36,520
We'll be signing up by dormitory.

81
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,720
Tell your dorm head

82
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,720
if you're interested.

83
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,760
That's all for today. Class dismissed.

84
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,960
Xiaoyu, I'll sign up.

85
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:41,600
Okay.

86
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:42,260
Signing up?

87
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,730
I've got zero athletic talent.

88
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:45,880
I thought

89
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:48,050
some people were just simple-minded,

90
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,010
but I didn't expect their limbs

91
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,860
to be underdeveloped too.

92
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,400
Stop running your mouth.

93
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,880
Does your dorm dare to send three people

94
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,340
and compete against ours?

95
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,720
Bring it on.

96
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,960
What, scared now?

97
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:07,560
Gu Han is at least
the basketball team captain.

98
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,600
How come you don't even dare

99
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,530
to participate in the sports meet?

100
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:13,080
And you claim you're good enough
for Gu Han?

101
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,960
We're talking about the sports meet.

102
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:16,420
Why drag others into this?

103
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,400
Are you signing up or not?

104
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,040
Our whole dorm is signing up.

105
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,400
Okay.

106
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:29,760
Write it down.

107
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,810
How long did it take?

108
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,930
Over 20 seconds.

109
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:42,400
Xiangxiang,
how many laps did you run this morning?

110
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,240
Two laps.

111
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,920
That's only 800 meters.

112
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:48,800
Show off for a moment,
suffer the consequences later.

113
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,000
Never heard that?

114
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,040
How does that saying go?

115
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,800
Haste makes waste.

116
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,480
The wind is too strong today.

117
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,680
Let's call it a day.

118
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,880
I agree.

119
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,240
You guys go back first.

120
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,400
I'll practice a bit more.

121
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,080
You're obsessed.

122
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:05,560
Let's go.

123
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,120
Let's go.

124
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,760
Isn't that Zhou Xiangxiang?

125
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,840
Running against such strong wind.

126
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:21,920
Impressive.

127
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,460
She deserves an award.

128
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,760
The "Courage Award."

129
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:27,850
Still laughing?

130
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,000
Look at your own

131
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,360
training performance.

132
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:31,280
Exactly.

133
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,330
You have the worst stamina.

134
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,140
Why is everyone picking on me?

135
00:06:35,159 --> 00:06:36,690
Said the wrong thing again.

136
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,000
Let's go. I'll walk you back to your dorm.

137
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,560
Okay.

138
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,920
Isn't that Gu Han?

139
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,800
Yeah.

140
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,890
What are you doing here?

141
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,610
Just passing by.

142
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,140
Here you go.

143
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:24,840
Did you buy this?

144
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,520
Someone gave it to the basketball team.

145
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,370
Giving the male players little bunny?

146
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:36,810
They probably thought
we had female players.

147
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,720
Take it. It's yours.

148
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,520
Okay.

149
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,840
It'll come in handy when I run.

150
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:47,480
Thanks.

151
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:49,520
So how's your training going?

152
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,600
Forget placing.

153
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,480
I can't even finish the run.

154
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:59,720
I really shouldn't have let Duan Xiaoyu
get under my skin.

155
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,920
Our team is doing outdoor
extra practices soon,

156
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:08,200
adding endurance drills.

157
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,400
If you...

158
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,900
Then good luck to you guys.

159
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,360
I'm sure you'll win.

160
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,080
Thanks.

161
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:27,970
[Gu Han]

162
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:30,680
Recently,

163
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:33,400
a female executive ran every day

164
00:08:32,130 --> 00:08:33,059
[39-year-old female executive
keeps running every day]

165
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,059
[Severe knee wear leaves her
unable to walk]

166
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:34,960
to keep a good figure.

167
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:38,080
After six months, she could barely walk,

168
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:38,900
[Sohu Running]

169
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,480
almost paralyzed.

170
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,559
It was because of her excessive mileage

171
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:43,280
and incorrect running form

172
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,880
that half of her patellofemoral cartilage

173
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:47,160
was worn away.

174
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:03,560
No way.

175
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:06,290
I've only run for one day.
It can't be that bad.

176
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,080
[Zhou Xiangxiang]

177
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,720
She's pushing herself too hard.

178
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,050
Are you okay?

179
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:51,860
You're gonna hurt yourself
training like this.

180
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,120
Be careful.

181
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,730
Let's continue.

182
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:55,800
Okay.

183
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:56,960
-Be careful.
-Let's go.

184
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,890
Alright, spread out into two rows.

185
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,640
Spread out. Spread out.

186
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,240
Wrists and ankles.

187
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,080
That's far enough.

188
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:07,600
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

189
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:09,600
Two, three, four, five.

190
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,720
Two, two, three, four, five.

191
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,660
[Sohu Running]

192
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,600
Because of incorrect running posture,

193
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,260
she nearly became paralyzed.

194
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:19,000
Three, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

195
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,320
Four, two, three, four.

196
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:23,520
Can I train with you guys?

197
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,080
Our training is really tough.

198
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,840
Are you sure?

199
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,300
I promise I won't hold everyone back.

200
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,800
Captain, just let her join.

201
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,500
Yeah, let Xiangxiang join us.

202
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:36,880
Go.

203
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:37,520
Okay.

204
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,560
Now, arms.

205
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:44,920
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

206
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:49,000
Two, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

207
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:49,760
Knees.

208
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:08,320
People usually overlook

209
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,680
the importance of warming up.

210
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:10,920
So by the end of a game,

211
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,360
our legs and feet cramp easily.

212
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,320
That's because

213
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:14,760
the warm-up isn't sufficient.

214
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,290
Our game has four quarters.

215
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,750
We need to properly control

216
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:20,150
the pace of offense
and defense in each one.

217
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:24,340
Next, let's talk about the essentials
of long-distance running.

218
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,080
That is...

219
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,600
pacing and breathing.

220
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:31,400
Is what the Captain said
related to the game?

221
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:34,480
Absolutely. It absolutely is.

222
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,240
As speed picks up,

223
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:38,680
fatigue rises and breathing gets heavier.

224
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,480
At this time,

225
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,680
you can adopt the method
of exhaling for one step

226
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,440
and inhaling for the next.

227
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,820
Pace yourself wisely.

228
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,460
Focus on exhaling.

229
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,760
Only after fully expelling carbon dioxide

230
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,560
can you take in enough oxygen.

231
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,240
I'll say it again.

232
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,880
The key to long-distance running

233
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:02,400
is pacing and breathing.

234
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:04,970
Understood?

235
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,280
Understood.

236
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,640
One, two, one, two, one, two.

237
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:10,520
Be neat.

238
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,800
One, two. One, two. One, two.

239
00:12:12,830 --> 00:12:17,110
One, two, one, two, one, two.

240
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:21,400
One, two, one, two, one, two.

241
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:24,090
One, two, one, two, one, two.

242
00:12:24,130 --> 00:12:25,160
Ready to speed up.

243
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,600
One, two, one, two, one, two.

244
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:29,950
One, two, one, two, one, two.

245
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,900
Watch your breathing.

246
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:33,330
One, two, one. One, two, one.
One, two, one.

247
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:36,230
One, two, one. One, two, one.
One, two, one.

248
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:39,130
The last one does shuttle runs.

249
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,420
One, two, one, two, one, two.

250
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,070
One, two, one, two, one, two.

251
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:45,950
One, two, one, two, one, two.

252
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,280
Time for stretching.

253
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:53,640
I can't. I can't.

254
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,770
Shuttle runs, ten sets.

255
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,520
Go.

256
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,680
I can't run anymore.

257
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,640
Go.

258
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:16,480
Can you run properly?

259
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:18,880
Ten more sets.

260
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:20,360
Go.

261
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:27,760
Come on.

262
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,000
Good stamina.

263
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,960
Stop pressing. It hurts.

264
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,960
No way.

265
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,200
She's got low blood sugar.

266
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,260
Come over and help.

267
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:58,800
Help, help, help.

268
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,200
Help.

269
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:13,480
Eat this.

270
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,130
Look at the Captain.

271
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,320
Next, get into pairs.

272
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,850
Stretching exercises.

273
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:32,880
What?

274
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,490
You need to stretch after running.

275
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:40,040
But I have low blood sugar.

276
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,160
I'm so dizzy.

277
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,280
So dizzy.

278
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:44,960
Let's go.

279
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,120
Here.

280
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,280
Hurry.

281
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,010
Come on, straighten your legs.

282
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,280
Okay, hands.

283
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:03,240
Come on.

284
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:07,360
I... I can do it myself.

285
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:08,900
It's just stretching.

286
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,000
How is it? Not bad, right?

287
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:27,560
Come on.

288
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:29,380
Relax.

289
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,210
Does it hurt?

290
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:36,810
It doesn't hurt.

291
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,320
I thought it would hurt a lot.

292
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:42,880
Relax, relax.

293
00:15:44,330 --> 00:15:45,000
Relax a bit.

294
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:47,960
Relax. Don't tense up.

295
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:49,540
Exhale.

296
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:50,240
Ow, ow, ow.

297
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:51,200
Ow, ow, ow.

298
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:51,760
Okay.

299
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,560
Slowly up, slowly up.

300
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:56,520
Slowly up.

301
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:57,680
Okay.

302
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,040
Okay, one more time.

303
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:13,880
Your turn.

304
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,180
I don't need to.

305
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,500
What do you mean you don't need to?

306
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:20,720
We agreed on partner work,

307
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,480
help each other out.

308
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:24,520
Come on.

309
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:28,240
Come on, sit properly.

310
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,080
Are you ready?

311
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:53,720
Why does it feel like nothing happened?

312
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,640
One more time.

313
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:23,480
Fine, you win.

314
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:34,760
Continue.

315
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,920
Xiangxiang, not bad,

316
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,120
you've kept up with us this whole time.

317
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:51,850
Yeah.

318
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:54,000
Didn't I tell you?

319
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:58,040
I will definitely not hold everyone back.

320
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,880
Xiangxiang, I have high hopes for you
in this race.

321
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:03,280
Gu Han, what do you think?

322
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,000
It'd be good enough if she can finish.

323
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,600
But since she trains with us,

324
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,720
we can't let her be a laughingstock.

325
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,200
Indirect kiss!

326
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,760
-She got Gu Han's saliva!
-Kiss! Kiss!

327
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,290
-Kiss! Kiss!
-Your saliva!

328
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:31,000
Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

329
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,160
Kiss.

330
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,920
Break's over. Leg day.

331
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,840
I have something to do. Excuse me.

332
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:41,640
My mom is visiting me today. Bye.

333
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:43,680
I have class.

334
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:19,020
[Gongxing Building]

335
00:19:22,690 --> 00:19:27,720
[Jiangcheng University TV Station]

336
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,520
You three

337
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,760
are already outstanding hosts

338
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,560
we've selected from our school.

339
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:36,280
If we compare a show to a dish,

340
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,160
the show's content is the main ingredient,

341
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,490
and the host's charisma is the seasoning.

342
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:42,280
Fang Yu is here.

343
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:42,960
Hello, Director.

344
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,640
-Hello, Senior.
-Hello, Senior.

345
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,440
Congratulations to you all.

346
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,070
Have a seat.

347
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:47,350
Your Senior Fang Yu

348
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,640
was interning at the city station
a few days ago.

349
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,900
We've been discussing

350
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,840
how to turn his internship experience

351
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:54,900
into a practical assignment for you.

352
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,370
Fang Yu, say a few words.

353
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:58,040
I think the city station's

354
00:19:58,040 --> 00:19:59,560
requirements for hosts

355
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,880
are becoming more diverse.

356
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,480
It's not just about

357
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:04,400
broadcasting news
in front of the camera anymore.

358
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,880
In fact, in most cases,

359
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:07,760
they get involved in news gathering

360
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:09,160
and writing.

361
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:10,840
For this practical assignment,

362
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:11,880
I suggest everyone

363
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:14,240
complete the gathering
and writing independently.

364
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:15,920
If you have any questions,

365
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,720
feel free to come ask me anytime.

366
00:20:17,890 --> 00:20:19,000
What are your thoughts?

367
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,480
Senior, you definitely have plenty
of experience in this area,

368
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:23,280
but we already have heavy
major coursework.

369
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:25,360
If we have to handle all on our own,

370
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:27,420
I'm afraid we won't have enough time.

371
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,880
I agree with Senior Fang Yu's proposal.

372
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,800
Once you join the campus TV station,

373
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,640
all the training and learning

374
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:35,640
is meant to help us

375
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,280
get on stage faster.

376
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:39,240
Cultivating directing and editing skills

377
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,840
is actually an extra gain

378
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:42,810
that we might not learn elsewhere.

379
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,360
Understanding the full show
production workflow

380
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:46,840
is really essential

381
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,440
for new hosts.

382
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:51,040
It helps us face audiences with confidence

383
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:52,610
and handle their feedback.

384
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:53,880
Xiangxiang is right.

385
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:55,480
I've also been thinking about

386
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:56,840
trying some new approaches

387
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,160
in our training.

388
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:02,160
Thanks for backing my idea just now.

389
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:04,240
You're welcome.

390
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,080
You're doing it for our own good.

391
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:08,680
For your independent documentary topic,

392
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:10,360
if you need any help from me,

393
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,680
just tell me.

394
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,760
After all, it's your first time.

395
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,120
I heard you signed up

396
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,560
for the 3,000-meter run.

397
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,040
I've known you for so long,

398
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:21,300
but I didn't expect you to be so athletic.

399
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,920
I don't have anything
this afternoon anyway.

400
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,880
How about we go to West Mountain again

401
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,600
and squeeze in a long-distance run

402
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:28,600
while we're at it?

403
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:29,480
Okay.

404
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:31,650
[Zhou Xiangxiang]

405
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:32,760
[Zhou Xiangxiang. Dialing]

406
00:21:35,150 --> 00:21:35,810
Hello.

407
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:37,640
Last-minute special training.

408
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,820
But I have something to do now.

409
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:41,680
That is crazy.

410
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,730
What's wrong? Is something up?

411
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:48,280
Sorry, Senior.

412
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,300
I have last-minute training.

413
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,610
Maybe next time.

414
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,920
It's okay. Go ahead.

415
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:57,920
Bye.

416
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:08,920
Get in.

417
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:11,960
Aren't we training? Where are the others?

418
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,740
Private training.

419
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:16,160
Get in.

420
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:20,960
Bag.

421
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:41,680
The training you mentioned

422
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:42,880
is mountain climbing?

423
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:44,680
Don't you like mountain climbing?

424
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:46,640
Who said I like mountain climbing?

425
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,360
Within 30 minutes,

426
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,240
if you don't reach the top,

427
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:51,900
you'll do another round trip.

428
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:55,800
No way. Climbing mountains is exhausting.

429
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:57,040
Climbing such a high mountain

430
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,880
will kill me.

431
00:22:59,110 --> 00:23:00,840
-Can we skip this?
-Three.

432
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:01,760
No.

433
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,960
-Two.
-I really cannot do this.

434
00:23:04,290 --> 00:23:05,030
One.

435
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:16,920
[Time]

436
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:20,010
One, two. One, two.

437
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:22,640
One, two. One, two.

438
00:23:22,670 --> 00:23:23,500
One.

439
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:27,800
Senior.

440
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:29,920
I'm just running 3,000 meters.

441
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:31,640
You don't have to take it so seriously.

442
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:33,160
Control your pace. Watch your breathing.

443
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:34,760
Don't let others affect you.

444
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:36,760
There's no one else here.

445
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:37,720
You ran too fast at the beginning.

446
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:39,850
That's why you're panting so much now.

447
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:42,320
Pace.

448
00:23:42,370 --> 00:23:43,670
One, two.

449
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:47,040
Inhale, exhale, inhale, exhale,
inhale, exhale.

450
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:47,750
Inhale.

451
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:48,800
Run.

452
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:50,600
Go.

453
00:23:51,760 --> 00:23:52,480
Run!

454
00:23:52,920 --> 00:23:56,070
[Time]

455
00:23:54,380 --> 00:23:57,000
One, two, one, two, one, two.

456
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,360
Keep going. We're almost there.

457
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:04,920
Don't stop.

458
00:24:06,240 --> 00:24:06,880
Breathe.

459
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:11,960
No, no, no.

460
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:15,000
My low blood sugar is acting up.

461
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:16,210
Low blood sugar?

462
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:18,680
So dizzy, so dizzy, so dizzy.

463
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:20,680
I'm so dizzy.

464
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:21,440
Hand.

465
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:25,240
Enough?

466
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,000
I didn't expect

467
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:36,920
you to be so well-prepared.

468
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:38,520
Eat it.

469
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:42,600
Suddenly I don't feel dizzy anymore.

470
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:43,280
Not dizzy?

471
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:45,680
Run.

472
00:24:48,470 --> 00:24:51,060
[Time]

473
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:49,970
Breathing and pace.

474
00:24:58,040 --> 00:24:59,320
How is it? Time?

475
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:04,370
One minute left.

476
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,560
I am really amazing!

477
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:10,200
Right?

478
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:12,080
You also think I'm amazing,

479
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:12,960
right?

480
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:15,000
I can definitely beat Duan Xiaoyu,

481
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:15,840
right?

482
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:21,040
You finally admit I'm amazing.

483
00:25:21,080 --> 00:25:22,560
I knew it!

484
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:36,080
Zhou Xiangxiang.

485
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:39,080
Will you still remember me
when you grow up?

486
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:41,000
Of course I will.

487
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:43,480
But people change when they grow up.

488
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,880
What if you don't recognize me someday?

489
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:49,080
Then redo all the things

490
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:50,400
we've been through together.

491
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:52,240
Help me remember you.

492
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:26,210
Will you come watch my race?

493
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:31,880
Let's see if you can get down the mountain

494
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:33,080
in half an hour first.

495
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:36,240
Oh no.

496
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:38,160
I only thought about climbing up,

497
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:39,760
but forgot about going down.

498
00:26:45,280 --> 00:26:46,080
What are you looking at?

499
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:47,680
Do you expect me to carry you?

500
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:55,480
Everyone,

501
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,960
today is the sports meet day

502
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:58,200
of our College of Liberal Arts.

503
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:59,280
Hello, babies.

504
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:00,040
We're right here

505
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:01,440
on JCU's sports field.

506
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:02,520
Our college's sports meet

507
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:03,720
is about to start.

508
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,880
I'm competing in the long‑jump too.

509
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:07,000
Wish us luck.

510
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:09,320
Here.

511
00:27:12,560 --> 00:27:13,600
So many things.

512
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:14,880
What's all in there?

513
00:27:15,080 --> 00:27:15,720
Since you're with me,

514
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:17,450
we can't compete without food.

515
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:18,320
Here.

516
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:20,520
Are you sure you're here to compete?

517
00:27:20,520 --> 00:27:21,480
Of course.

518
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:22,360
Before the competition,

519
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:24,040
mindset is very important.

520
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:26,520
Here, eat.

521
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:27,600
For you.

522
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:29,200
Eat well, everyone.

523
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:30,840
You need energy to compete.

524
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:33,720
Let's take a photo.

525
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:34,440
Sure.

526
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:37,640
Three, two, one.

527
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,920
The competition is about to start,

528
00:27:44,920 --> 00:27:46,920
and they're still snacking.

529
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:48,880
They clearly look down on us.

530
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:51,880
Zhou Xiangxiang.

531
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:55,120
You guys are pretty relaxed.

532
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:57,880
Monitor, why so fired up?

533
00:27:57,920 --> 00:28:00,080
Here, have some water to cool off.

534
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:01,120
Stop showing off.

535
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,040
Don't cry when you lose later.

536
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:05,480
Don't talk big.

537
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:06,760
Nobody knows how the race

538
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:07,680
will turn out.

539
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:09,210
When the time comes,

540
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:10,880
don't get lapped by me.

541
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:13,360
Imagine how funny

542
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:15,370
Senior Fang Yu would find that.

543
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:17,080
Senior Fang.

544
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:20,940
There you guys are.

545
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:24,360
How's the preparation going?

546
00:28:24,360 --> 00:28:25,160
Not bad.

547
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:26,450
What about you guys?

548
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:33,800
The women's 100-meter sprint
is about to begin.

549
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:36,200
All athletes, please report to the track

550
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,480
-and get ready.
-100 meters isn't that long.

551
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:39,080
Isn't it long?

552
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:40,600
Just don't be nervous.

553
00:28:40,640 --> 00:28:42,970
-You'll be fine once it's over.
-Xiaotao.

554
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:44,240
Thank you, Senior.

555
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:44,920
Don't get nervous

556
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:45,800
when you run.

557
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:46,480
Just relax.

558
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,980
Come on, Xiaotao!

559
00:28:57,010 --> 00:28:58,730
Come on, Xiaotao!

560
00:28:58,760 --> 00:29:00,390
Come on, Xiaotao!

561
00:29:00,410 --> 00:29:02,150
Come on, Xiaotao!

562
00:29:02,170 --> 00:29:03,760
Come on, Xiaotao!

563
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:06,280
Go, go, go!

564
00:29:06,280 --> 00:29:07,560
-Exaggerating.
-Come on!

565
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:09,440
Come on, Mihua!

566
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:11,840
Come on, Mihua!

567
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,440
Come on, Mihua!

568
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:17,440
-Come on, Xiaotao!
-Mihua, come on!

569
00:29:17,480 --> 00:29:19,040
On your marks!

570
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:23,160
Set!

571
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,600
-Go, Xiaotao!
-Go! Go!

572
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:31,800
-Mihua, come on!
-Xiaotao, come on!

573
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,360
-Go! Go!
-Go, Mihua!

574
00:29:34,360 --> 00:29:36,840
-Xiaotao, come on!
-Mihua!

575
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:39,680
Come on, Xiaotao!

576
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:41,000
Come on, Xiaotao!

577
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:43,080
Come on, Xiaotao!

578
00:29:44,280 --> 00:29:45,240
Come on!

579
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:46,960
Come on, Mihua!

580
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:47,760
Come on!

581
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:53,720
Mihua, hold on!

582
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:57,640
Come on, Xiaotao!

583
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:02,480
I'll treat you all to dinner tonight

584
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:03,640
to make up for this.

585
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:05,170
We didn't lose face.

586
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:07,680
I just can't stand their smug looks.

587
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:08,760
It's okay.

588
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:11,290
You has long legs. She'll definitely win.

589
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,280
You!

590
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:23,280
Xinyi!

591
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:25,280
What's wrong? What happened?

592
00:30:25,280 --> 00:30:27,240
You twisted her ankle and got injured.

593
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:28,570
Then let's go together.

594
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:29,960
Um, Xiaotao,

595
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:31,200
you stay with Xiangxiang for the race.

596
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:32,520
I'll let you two know if anything happens.

597
00:30:32,520 --> 00:30:34,040
-OK. Hurry over.
-Okay.

598
00:30:34,280 --> 00:30:34,880
Be careful.

599
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:35,520
Okay.

600
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:39,320
I just lost the race,

601
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,640
and You sprained her ankle.

602
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:42,080
What rotten luck.

603
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,480
You'll be the only one left soon.

604
00:30:48,480 --> 00:30:49,280
Come on.

605
00:30:51,040 --> 00:30:51,760
Come on.

606
00:30:58,880 --> 00:30:59,600
Look at them.

607
00:30:59,600 --> 00:31:01,040
-0 to 2.
-How can they compete with us?

608
00:31:01,040 --> 00:31:02,880
We lost to their dorm again.

609
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:06,800
Did we lose?

610
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,880
What do you mean?

611
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:11,760
You know what Duan Xiaoyu is like.

612
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:14,520
She doesn't care if others win or lose.

613
00:31:14,520 --> 00:31:15,960
She just wants to win.

614
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:17,880
If I beat her this time,

615
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:19,680
she'll never bring up

616
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:21,880
what happened today
for the rest of her life.

617
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:22,640
Right.

618
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:25,000
So your race with her is the key.

619
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:29,230
All women's 3000‑meter runners,

620
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:30,720
-please head to the starting line.
-Come on, Xiangxiang!

621
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:31,720
Run her into tears.

622
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:33,200
I'll make hot pot noodles for you tonight.

623
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:34,760
Okay, I'll go get ready.

624
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:35,480
Go!

625
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:43,730
You still haven't given up?

626
00:31:43,760 --> 00:31:45,290
Your dorm has already lost.

627
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:49,160
I haven't lost to you yet.

628
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:50,760
Just you wait.

629
00:31:56,360 --> 00:31:57,480
On your marks!

630
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,120
Set!

631
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:02,080
Go Xiangxiang!

632
00:32:02,680 --> 00:32:03,540
Go Xiangxiang!

633
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:04,600
Go, go!
